---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { SITE } from "../../data/site";
---
<BaseLayout title="Shipping Guide: FBA vs Express vs Sea" description="Compare DHL express, Amazon FBA, and sea freight for activewear. Find the cheapest and fastest option for your business size and sales volume.">
  <section style="background:var(--color-primary);color:white;">
    <div style="max-width:56rem;margin:0 auto;padding:4rem 1.5rem;text-align:center;">
      <div style="display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;gap:0.75rem;margin-bottom:0.75rem;">
        <span style="font-size:1.5rem;">🚢</span>
        <span style="font-size:0.75rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--color-accent-light);background:rgba(255,255,255,0.1);padding:0.2rem 0.75rem;border-radius:9999px;">All Levels</span>
        <span style="font-size:0.75rem;color:#94a3b8;">9 min read</span>
      </div>
      <h1 style="font-size:2.25rem;font-weight:800;margin-bottom:1rem;">Shipping Guide: FBA vs Express vs Sea</h1>
      <p style="color:#94a3b8;max-width:42rem;margin:0 auto;">Compare DHL express, Amazon FBA, and sea freight for activewear. Find the cheapest and fastest option for your business size and sales volume.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div style="max-width:56rem;margin:0 auto;padding:2.5rem 1.5rem;">
    <div style="background:white;border:1px solid var(--color-border);border-radius:1rem;padding:2rem;margin-bottom:2rem;">
      
      <h2 style="font-size:1.25rem;font-weight:800;color:var(--color-primary);margin-top:2rem;margin-bottom:0.75rem;">The 3 Main Shipping Options</h2>
      <p style="font-size:0.95rem;color:var(--color-text-light);line-height:1.8;">Activewear is relatively light (a pair of leggings weighs 200-350g), so shipping costs are manageable compared to bulky items. Your three main options: (1) Express courier (DHL, FedEx, UPS) - fastest, most expensive. Best for samples, urgent orders, and small quantities. (2) FBA (Amazon fulfillment) - integrates with your Amazon store, adds fulfillment fees but handles storage and delivery. (3) Sea freight + air freight - cheapest for large volumes, slowest for sea (15-25 days). Best for bulk orders of 500+ pieces.</p>
      
      
      <h2 style="font-size:1.25rem;font-weight:800;color:var(--color-primary);margin-top:2rem;margin-bottom:0.75rem;">Express Courier (DHL / FedEx / UPS)</h2>
      <p style="font-size:0.95rem;color:var(--color-text-light);line-height:1.8;">Delivery time: 3-7 business days worldwide. Cost: $4-8 per unit for 50-100 pieces. Best for: samples, test orders, small quantities under 500 pieces, urgent restocking. How it works: factory ships directly to your address. You pay duties and taxes upon arrival. Pros: fast, door-to-door, no minimum. Cons: expensive per unit, you handle customs.</p>
      
      
      <h2 style="font-size:1.25rem;font-weight:800;color:var(--color-primary);margin-top:2rem;margin-bottom:0.75rem;">Amazon FBA (Fulfilled by Amazon)</h2>
      <p style="font-size:0.95rem;color:var(--color-text-light);line-height:1.8;">Delivery time: 7-14 days (sea to Amazon warehouse) + 1-2 days (Amazon to customer). Cost: $2-5 per unit for shipping to FBA warehouse + $3-6 fulfillment fee per unit. Best for: Amazon sellers with consistent monthly volume of 200+ pieces. How it works: ship in bulk to Amazon warehouse, Amazon handles storage, picking, packing, and last-mile delivery. Pros: Prime eligibility, customer service handled by Amazon. Cons: Storage fees, long-term storage fees after 6 months, risk of stranded inventory.</p>
      
      
      <h2 style="font-size:1.25rem;font-weight:800;color:var(--color-primary);margin-top:2rem;margin-bottom:0.75rem;">Sea Freight for Bulk Orders</h2>
      <p style="font-size:0.95rem;color:var(--color-text-light);line-height:1.8;">Delivery time: 15-25 days to major ports. Cost: $1-2 per unit for 500+ pieces. Best for: established sellers with capital to hold inventory, seasonal buyers, Amazon FBA bulk senders. How it works: 20ft container holds approximately 5,000-8,000 pieces of activewear. You need a freight forwarder to handle customs clearance and last-mile delivery. Pros: dramatically reduces per-unit shipping cost. Cons: requires 1,000+ piece orders to make sense, 3-4 week lead time, capital tied up in transit.</p>
      
      
      <h2 style="font-size:1.25rem;font-weight:800;color:var(--color-primary);margin-top:2rem;margin-bottom:0.75rem;">How to Choose the Right Shipping Method</h2>
      <p style="font-size:0.95rem;color:var(--color-text-light);line-height:1.8;">undefined</p>
      <ul style="margin-top:0.75rem;padding-left:1.5rem;font-size:0.9rem;color:var(--color-text-light);line-height:1.8;"><li style="margin-bottom:0.4rem;">Under 50 pieces: Express courier only (DHL/FedEx)</li><li style="margin-bottom:0.4rem;">50-500 pieces: Express courier or air freight (cheaper than express for this range)</li><li style="margin-bottom:0.4rem;">500-2,000 pieces: Sea freight to a freight forwarder, then last-mile delivery</li><li style="margin-bottom:0.4rem;">2,000+ pieces: FBA sea freight send or dedicated sea container</li><li style="margin-bottom:0.4rem;">Always get 3 shipping quotes before committing - freight forwarders vary wildly in pricing</li></ul>
      
    </div>

    <h2 style="font-size:1.5rem;font-weight:800;color:var(--color-primary);margin-bottom:1.25rem;text-align:center;">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
    <div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:0.75rem;margin-bottom:2.5rem;">
      
      <details style="background:white;border:1px solid var(--color-border);border-radius:0.75rem;overflow:hidden;">
        <summary style="display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;padding:1rem 1.25rem;cursor:pointer;list-style:none;gap:1rem;">
          <span style="font-weight:600;color:var(--color-text);font-size:0.9rem;">What are the total costs for shipping activewear from China?</span>
          <svg style="width:1.25rem;height:1.25rem;color:var(--color-text-light);flex-shrink:0;" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7"/></svg>
        </summary>
        <div style="padding:0.75rem 1.25rem 1.25rem;font-size:0.875rem;color:var(--color-text-light);line-height:1.7;border-top:1px solid var(--color-border);">Per-unit shipping costs vary by method: Express (50-100pcs) costs $4-8/unit, Air freight (100-500pcs) costs $2-4/unit, Sea freight (500+pcs) costs $1-2/unit. Plus: customs duties (10-12% for USA, 12% for EU on activewear), import VAT (UK 20%, EU 19-27%), and freight forwarder fees ($150-300 per shipment). Always get a landed cost quote that includes all fees.</div>
      </details>
      
      <details style="background:white;border:1px solid var(--color-border);border-radius:0.75rem;overflow:hidden;">
        <summary style="display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;padding:1rem 1.25rem;cursor:pointer;list-style:none;gap:1rem;">
          <span style="font-weight:600;color:var(--color-text);font-size:0.9rem;">Do I pay customs duties when shipping to Amazon FBA?</span>
          <svg style="width:1.25rem;height:1.25rem;color:var(--color-text-light);flex-shrink:0;" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7"/></svg>
        </summary>
        <div style="padding:0.75rem 1.25rem 1.25rem;font-size:0.875rem;color:var(--color-text-light);line-height:1.7;border-top:1px solid var(--color-border);">Yes. All imports to the US pay customs duties. Activewear typically falls under HTS code 6114.30 with a duty rate of 10-12%. Amazon does not pay import duties on your behalf - you are responsible for all applicable fees. Amazon may hold or delay shipments that arrive without proper documentation.</div>
      </details>
      
      <details style="background:white;border:1px solid var(--color-border);border-radius:0.75rem;overflow:hidden;">
        <summary style="display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;padding:1rem 1.25rem;cursor:pointer;list-style:none;gap:1rem;">
          <span style="font-weight:600;color:var(--color-text);font-size:0.9rem;">How long does it take to ship activewear from China?</span>
          <svg style="width:1.25rem;height:1.25rem;color:var(--color-text-light);flex-shrink:0;" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7"/></svg>
        </summary>
        <div style="padding:0.75rem 1.25rem 1.25rem;font-size:0.875rem;color:var(--color-text-light);line-height:1.7;border-top:1px solid var(--color-border);">Express: 3-7 business days door-to-door. Air freight: 5-10 days (warehouse to warehouse). Sea freight: 15-25 days (port to port), plus 3-7 days for customs clearance and last-mile delivery. FBA sea freight: 20-35 days from factory to Amazon warehouse. Always add 3-5 days buffer for potential delays.</div>
      </details>
      
      <details style="background:white;border:1px solid var(--color-border);border-radius:0.75rem;overflow:hidden;">
        <summary style="display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;padding:1rem 1.25rem;cursor:pointer;list-style:none;gap:1rem;">
          <span style="font-weight:600;color:var(--color-text);font-size:0.9rem;">What is a freight forwarder and do I need one?</span>
          <svg style="width:1.25rem;height:1.25rem;color:var(--color-text-light);flex-shrink:0;" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7"/></svg>
        </summary>
        <div style="padding:0.75rem 1.25rem 1.25rem;font-size:0.875rem;color:var(--color-text-light);line-height:1.7;border-top:1px solid var(--color-border);">A freight forwarder handles logistics for international shipping: negotiating with carriers, booking space, handling customs paperwork, and arranging last-mile delivery. For express shipping under 500 pieces, you typically do not need one. For sea freight or FBA shipments over 500 pieces, a freight forwarder is essential. Popular options: Flexport, Freightos, and local Chinese forwarders like Allwin.</div>
      </details>
      
      <details style="background:white;border:1px solid var(--color-border);border-radius:0.75rem;overflow:hidden;">
        <summary style="display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;padding:1rem 1.25rem;cursor:pointer;list-style:none;gap:1rem;">
          <span style="font-weight:600;color:var(--color-text);font-size:0.9rem;">How do I reduce shipping costs?</span>
          <svg style="width:1.25rem;height:1.25rem;color:var(--color-text-light);flex-shrink:0;" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7"/></svg>
        </summary>
        <div style="padding:0.75rem 1.25rem 1.25rem;font-size:0.875rem;color:var(--color-text-light);line-height:1.7;border-top:1px solid var(--color-border);">Three strategies: (1) Consolidate shipments - combine multiple supplier orders into one container to save on freight costs. (2) Negotiate with freight forwarders - get quotes from 3-5 forwarders and ask for volume discounts. (3) Ship during off-peak seasons (January-March) when container rates are 20-40% lower than peak season (September-November).</div>
      </details>
      
    </div>

    <div style="background:var(--color-secondary);border-radius:1.5rem;padding:2rem;text-align:center;">
      <h2 style="font-size:1.25rem;font-weight:800;color:var(--color-primary);margin-bottom:0.5rem;">Have More Questions?</h2>
      <p style="font-size:0.875rem;color:var(--color-text-light);margin-bottom:1.25rem;">Get personalized answers for your specific business on WhatsApp.</p>
      <a href={SITE.whatsappLink} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:0.5rem;background:var(--color-whatsapp);color:white;padding:0.875rem 2rem;border-radius:9999px;font-weight:700;">Ask on WhatsApp</a>
    </div>
  </div>

  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify({
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "FAQPage",
    "mainEntity": [
    {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "What are the total costs for shipping activewear from China?",
        "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Per-unit shipping costs vary by method: Express (50-100pcs) costs $4-8/unit, Air freight (100-500pcs) costs $2-4/unit, Sea freight (500+pcs) costs $1-2/unit. Plus: customs duties (10-12% for USA, 12% for EU on activewear), import VAT (UK 20%, EU 19-27%), and freight forwarder fees ($150-300 per shipment). Always get a landed cost quote that includes all fees."
        }
    },
    {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "Do I pay customs duties when shipping to Amazon FBA?",
        "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Yes. All imports to the US pay customs duties. Activewear typically falls under HTS code 6114.30 with a duty rate of 10-12%. Amazon does not pay import duties on your behalf - you are responsible for all applicable fees. Amazon may hold or delay shipments that arrive without proper documentation."
        }
    },
    {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "How long does it take to ship activewear from China?",
        "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Express: 3-7 business days door-to-door. Air freight: 5-10 days (warehouse to warehouse). Sea freight: 15-25 days (port to port), plus 3-7 days for customs clearance and last-mile delivery. FBA sea freight: 20-35 days from factory to Amazon warehouse. Always add 3-5 days buffer for potential delays."
        }
    },
    {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "What is a freight forwarder and do I need one?",
        "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "A freight forwarder handles logistics for international shipping: negotiating with carriers, booking space, handling customs paperwork, and arranging last-mile delivery. For express shipping under 500 pieces, you typically do not need one. For sea freight or FBA shipments over 500 pieces, a freight forwarder is essential. Popular options: Flexport, Freightos, and local Chinese forwarders like Allwin."
        }
    },
    {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "How do I reduce shipping costs?",
        "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Three strategies: (1) Consolidate shipments - combine multiple supplier orders into one container to save on freight costs. (2) Negotiate with freight forwarders - get quotes from 3-5 forwarders and ask for volume discounts. (3) Ship during off-peak seasons (January-March) when container rates are 20-40% lower than peak season (September-November)."
        }
    }
],
  })} />
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify({
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
    "itemListElement": [
      { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 1, "name": "Home", "item": SITE.url },
      { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 2, "name": "Resources", "item": SITE.url + "/resources" },
      { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 3, "name": "Shipping Guide: FBA vs Express vs Sea", "item": SITE.url + "/resources/shipping-guide-fba-express" },
    ],
  })} />
</BaseLayout>
